  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase changes: 1090 K, melting point of Eu; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.202$ kcal/mol.\n1800 K, boiling point of Eu; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 34.585$ kcal/mol \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o = 8.431 + 0.314x10^{-3}T - 0.848x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o - H_{298}^o = 8.431x10^{-3}T + 0.157x10^{-6}T^2 + 0.848x10^2T^{-1} - 2.812$ </td></tr></table>\nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1090 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -14.436 + 0.520 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 2.375 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 146.800 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -14.436 - 0.520 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 2.375 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 73.400 \\text{T}^{-1} = 15.597 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1090-1800 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -14.022 - 4.294 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.094 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 62.200 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -14.022 + 4.294 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.094 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 31.100 \\text{T}^{-1} = 47.125 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1800-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -56.835 + 0.736 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.350 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 62.200 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -56.835 - 0.736 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.350 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 31.100 \\text{T}^{-1} + 13.904 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
